  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When you say \"total overtime hours per month for the entire workforce cannot exceed 20 hours per worker,\" do you mean that each individual worker is limited to 20 overtime hours per month (so the total overtime capacity is 20 times the number of workers in that month), or that the sum of all overtime hours across the entire workforce is capped at a fixed 20 hours per month?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single clarification regarding the interpretation of the overtime constraint, presenting two mutually exclusive options for the same policy definition."
}

